# local-llamacpp-cpu-2b-q4_0 — authoritative configuration.
#
# The directory name is documentation; this file decides. Never copy a slot value
# out of the directory name into a CLI flag (NAMING.md, "The name is a claim").
#
# Committed on purpose and deliberately NOT gitignored. A real environment
# variable always wins over it: Makefiles use ?= and dotenv does not overwrite.
#
# The file is named tpu.env for consistency with every sibling. There is no TPU,
# no GPU and no cloud here.
#
# STATUS 2026-09-22: SERVING on f95b0d9. HOST HARDWARE CORRECTED; SWEEP QUARANTINED.
# Until 2026-09-15 this directory was a byte-identical copy of
# local-llamacpp-1650ti-2b-q4_0. Values below that came from that rig were
# measured on a GPU; KV_CACHE_TYPE and FLASH_ATTENTION are still UNMEASURED here.
# THREADS and THREADS_BATCH were briefly believed measured; that sweep is
# quarantined and they are now derived-plus-spot-checked — see their comment.
# llama.cpp is built CPU-only at the commit recorded below and the GGUF is at
# MODEL_PATH.
#
# 2026-09-22: the host moved to Debian sid (gcc 16.2, CUDA 13.4) and both arms were
# rebuilt from clean onto f95b0d9. In the course of that the CPU identity in this
# file was found to be wrong in every field — see the Hardware block. The 18-cell
# thread/affinity sweep describes a 4P+8E die this machine is not, and is
# quarantined; THREADS/THREADS_BATCH have been re-derived for the real topology.
# Treat this rig as having NO valid absolute measurements until a
# thermally-controlled sweep is re-run on f95b0d9.

# ── Model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL_NAME is the upstream artifact; MODEL_PATH is what llama.cpp opens. The
# GGUF lives outside the git work tree on purpose.
MODEL_NAME=google/gemma-4-E2B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf
MODEL_PATH=/home/xbill/models/gemma-4-E2B-it-qat-q4_0/gemma-4-E2B_q4_0-it.gguf

# Slot 5 of the directory name. Reads off MODEL_NAME, not off the file's
# dominant tensor type — which is Q6_K, not Q4_0. See CLAUDE.md.
QUANTIZATION=q4_0

# ── Hardware ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RE-MEASURED 2026-09-22 from lscpu, /proc/cpuinfo, /proc/meminfo, dmidecode and
# /sys/devices/cpu_{core,atom}. EVERY FIELD IN THIS BLOCK WAS WRONG until then.
#
# It said i7-1360P, 12 cores / 16 threads, hybrid 4 P + 8 E at logical 0-15, with
# avx_vnni. The kernel says otherwise and the kernel is the authority: this is a
# Lenovo Yoga 9 15IMH5 (DMI 82DE) with a Comet Lake i7-10750H — 6 physical cores,
# 12 logical, HOMOGENEOUS, no P/E split, and NO avx_vnni. /sys/devices/cpu_core
# and /sys/devices/cpu_atom do not exist here; that absence is the P/E test.
#
# The 1360P never fitted the rest of the machine: no 1360P laptop ships a GTX
# 1650 Ti Max-Q, and local-pytorch-cpu-2b/CLAUDE.md said "6 physical cores and six
# SMT siblings" all along — exactly right — and was overruled by this file.
#
# THIS INVALIDATES benchmarks/runs/2026-09-16-thread-sweep-cpu. Its own
# results/topology.json records 16 online CPUs, hybrid=true, 4 perf cores; its
# topology.py re-run on this host today emits 12 CPUs, hybrid=0, 6 cores, and an
# EMPTY effiency set. The 0xFF00 "E-cores only" cell cannot exist here. That run
# did not come off this machine and is quarantined in its REPORT.md.
ACCELERATOR_TYPE=cpu
CPU_MODEL="Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz"
CPU_CORES=6
CPU_THREADS=12
# Homogeneous Comet Lake. SMT siblings pair as (0,6) (1,7) ... (5,11) — the second
# thread of core N is N+6, NOT N*2+1. Any mask written for a P/E die pins wrong.
CPU_P_CORE_LOGICAL=0-11
CPU_E_CORE_LOGICAL=
# avx avx2. NO avx512 and NO avx_vnni — avx_vnni arrived with Alder Lake, and this
# is the generation before it. Do not assume VNNI-accelerated int8 kernels.
CPU_SIMD="avx2"
HOST_RAM_GIB=15
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1

# ── Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A CPU-only build: GGML_CUDA=OFF. `make build` produces it. It is a separate
# build directory from any GPU build on purpose — start_model_server refuses a
# binary that has a GPU backend next to it or linked into it.
LLAMA_CPP_DIR=/home/xbill/llama.cpp
# BOTH ARMS OF THE CONTROL BUILD FROM THIS COMMIT, and that is the whole reason
# it is pinned. local-llamacpp-1650ti-2b-q4_0 was at 95ef7fc and this rig at
# 82324fc50, so differencing them would have carried an upstream delta inside
# what was supposed to be a device delta. Rebuilt both 2026-09-16, and again
# 2026-09-22 onto f95b0d9 (100 commits on from c6824a9) after the host moved to
# Debian sid: gcc 16.2.0, CUDA 13.4. Both arms reconfigured from clean — the old
# CMakeCaches still recorded gcc 14 and CUDA 13.3 — and both verified: the GPU
# arm lists CUDA0, this one lists no devices at all.
#
# EVERY MEASUREMENT IN THIS RIG PREDATES THE INSTALLED BINARY. The 18 thread-sweep
# cells and the 8 paired-sweep cells were measured on 82324fc50 and c6824a9; the
# binary here is now f95b0d9, built by a different compiler. The conclusions
# (threads weak, affinity the real lever) are about this host and are not expected
# to move, but no absolute figure in benchmarks/ came off the binary now installed.
# Re-run before quoting one against anything measured after this line.
LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT=f95b0d9
LLAMA_SERVER_BIN=/home/xbill/llama.cpp/build-cpu/bin/llama-server

# ── Serving ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The endpoint is not discovered; it is known before the process starts.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8080
ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# NOT configurable. `-ngl 0` and an empty CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES are hardcoded in
# both `make serve` and server.py, because a CPU rig that can be flipped onto a
# GPU by one env line measures whichever device happened to be present.

# 18 KiB/token geometry (MODELS.md), but llama.cpp caps the 12 sliding layers at
# the 1024-cell window, so KV at 8192 is ~60 MiB, not 144 (MEASURED on the 1650ti
# sibling from the allocation log). Host RAM is not the constraint at this size.
CONTEXT_SIZE=8192

# UNMEASURED ON CPU. f16 is kept because the q8_0 regression was measured on the
# GPU sibling and the KV is tiny either way; whether dequant costs the same on
# AVX2 is an open question, not a settled one.
KV_CACHE_TYPE=f16

# UNMEASURED ON CPU. The +4.8% was a CUDA result.
FLASH_ATTENTION=1

# Prometheus metrics at $ENDPOINT/metrics. Operational visibility only — never
# the benchmark decode column (see CLAUDE.md).
METRICS=1

# RE-DERIVED 2026-09-22 FOR THE REAL TOPOLOGY. The old 4/8 were |decode set| and
# |prefill set| of a 4P+8E die that is not this machine (see the Hardware block),
# and the sweep that blessed them is quarantined. On an i7-10750H the same
# derivation — one thread per physical core for decode, every logical for prefill
# — gives 6 and 12, which is what these are.
#
# SPOT-CHECKED, NOT SWEPT. llama-bench, f95b0d9, pp512/tg128, r=2, one invocation
# so the three cells share a thermal state:
#     -t 4   pp512 78.74   tg128 17.72
#     -t 6   pp512 89.32   tg128 17.53
#     -t 12  pp512 93.42   tg128 15.54
# The direction is clear and matches the derivation: prefill scales with threads
# (+18.6% from 4 to 12), decode does not and is HURT by SMT (-12.3% at 12). Decode
# at 4 vs 6 is a 1.1% difference; 6 is kept because it follows from the topology
# rather than from a tie-break.
#
# DO NOT TREAT THOSE ABSOLUTES AS A MEASUREMENT. This host thermally throttles
# hard — 28,271 package throttle events, 74C before the check and 92C after — and
# an IDENTICAL config re-run cold moved 19% on decode (tg128 17.70 -> 14.29 at
# -t 6 -C 0x3F). Run-to-run drift here is larger than every lever measured. A real
# sweep needs cooldowns between cells and interleaved ordering; until then no
# absolute t/s from this rig means anything.
THREADS=6
THREADS_BATCH=12

# One interactive session. llama.cpp SPLITS --ctx-size ACROSS SLOTS, so raising
# this without raising CONTEXT_SIZE shrinks each sequence.
PARALLEL_SLOTS=1

# ── CPU affinity: STILL NOT A KEY, AND NO LONGER A MEASURED 1.61x ────────────
# What stood here until 2026-09-22 described a 4 P-core + 8 E-core die: E-cores as
# stragglers, 0x55 as "one thread per P-core", a 1.61x prefill swing. THIS HOST HAS
# NO E-CORES. It is a homogeneous 6-core i7-10750H, so there is no straggler class
# to exclude and that whole mechanism does not apply here. The masks it named are
# actively wrong on this die: 0x55 is cpus 0,2,4,6 — and cpu6 is the SMT SIBLING
# of cpu0 — so it pins to 3 physical cores with one of them doubled.
#
# THE RULE SURVIVES; THE NUMBERS DO NOT. A hex mask is a fact about one die, never
# configuration, and freezing one here is the same mistake as copying a
# directory-name slot into a CLI flag. Derive it, the way cpu_status already
# re-reads topology:
#   prefill set = /sys/devices/cpu_core/cpus     (absent => homogeneous
#                                                 => all online CPUs)
#   decode  set = lowest of each distinct
#                 /sys/.../cpu<N>/topology/thread_siblings_list within that set
#   mask        = sum(1 << cpu)
# On THIS host that yields 0xFFF (12 logical) and 0x3F (6 physical) — not 0xFF and
# 0x55 — which is exactly how the rule should degrade with no hybrid split.
# benchmarks/runs/2026-09-16-thread-sweep-cpu/topology.py implements it. Run it;
# never transcribe its output into this file.
#
# WHETHER PINNING BUYS ANYTHING HERE IS NOW OPEN. Spot-check 2026-09-22 measured
# -t 6 -C 0x3F at pp512 94.32 against 89.32 unpinned, then re-measured that SAME
# cell cold at 83.98. The 19% run-to-run drift swamps the 5% it was trying to show,
# so nothing is claimed either way. server.py still passes no affinity flags, and
# that is now gated on a thermally-controlled sweep, not merely on an end-to-end
# confirmation. llama-server spells it -C/--cpu-strict and -Cb/--cpu-strict-batch.
